Specification Investments

Description Tracking what an investment account is currently worth, without
# tracking lots, holding periods or realised gains.
Details
# SCOPE. The first round is about spending reports. No report in this file
# is compared against Quicken in that round, and the holdings report at
# the end of it is the last thing to build, not the first.
#
# What is in scope is everything in here that a spending report depends
# on, and that is more than it looks. The 899 investment records in the
# business file include dividends, which post to an income category, and
# fees, which post to an expense one. Those reach the spending report and
# must be right. So must the rule that sends a revaluation to
# Equity:Market Value Changes, because its whole purpose is to keep market
# movement out of that report.
#
# What can wait is the holdings report, the staleness marking, and
# recording prices at all. A migrated book has no price list to work from
# anyway, so every holding starts stale and the balances are as good as
# the last transaction makes them. See ImportQif and
# AcceptanceAgainstQuicken.
#
# What is wanted here is the current balance. Cost basis, holding periods
# and realised gain or loss are reported on the 1099, and keeping a second
# set of those figures here would mean maintaining something that has to
# agree with a document nobody controls. So they are not kept.
#
# What is kept must still balance, because the book is double entry
# throughout and net worth is read off the real accounts. A security is
# therefore an account of type Investment beneath the brokerage account,
# carrying a money balance like any other, and a share count beside it.
# When a price changes, the difference is posted against
# Equity:Market Value Changes. Equity is nominal, so a revaluation moves
# net worth without ever appearing in a report of income and expenses.
# That is the whole of the design, and it is what the simplification buys.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The shape of a brokerage account
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Background A brokerage account with two holdings
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                           | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Brokerage               | Brokerage  | true        |
| Assets:Brokerage:Cash          | Brokerage  | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX         | Brokerage  | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B         | Brokerage  | false       |
| Assets:Checking                | Checking   | false       |
| Income:Dividends               | Income     | false       |
| Income:Interest                | Income     | false       |
| Expenses:Investment:Fees       | Expense    | false       |
| Equity:Market Value Changes    | Equity     | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances        | Equity     | false       |

Entity Holding
Description The share count and price of one security, beside the account that
# carries its value.
Details Value is not stored. It is the money balance of the account, and the
# invariant below is what keeps the two in step.
# A security is identified by its name. The symbol is optional, because a
# QIF export generally has none: see the naming rule below.
| Attribute    | Type         | Default    | Notes                         |
| Account      | AccountPath  |            | The Investment account for it |
| SecurityName | SecurityName |            | The identifier                |
| Symbol       | Symbol       | none       | Optional shorthand            |
| Shares       | Shares       | 0          |                               |
| Price        | Price        | 0          | The last price recorded       |
| PriceAsOf    | Date         | 2024-01-01 | When that price was recorded  |

BusinessRule What the account of a holding is called
Description The symbol where there is one, because it is shorter and is what a
# holdings report is read by. The name otherwise.
Details Colons are replaced, as for any account name. A name of 76 characters
# makes a long path, and that is preferred to inventing a symbol that
Description would then disagree with every statement.
Examples: HoldingAccountName
| SecurityName                   | Symbol | AccountName                    |
| Vanguard Total Stock Mkt Idx   | VTSAX  | VTSAX                          |
| ISHARES U S TRANSPORTATION ETF |        | ISHARES U S TRANSPORTATION ETF |
| Berkshire Hathaway B           | BRK.B  | BRK.B                          |

Attributes HoldingAccountName
| Attribute    | Type         | Default |
| SecurityName | SecurityName |         |
| Symbol       | Symbol       | none    |
| AccountName  | AccountName  |         |

Collection Holdings
| DataType | Minimum | Maximum | Notes                        |
| Holding  | 0       | 10000   | One per Investment account   |

BusinessRule The value of a holding is its shares times its price
Description And that value is the money balance of its account. Every operation
# below leaves this true; it is checked whenever the file is opened.
Details Rounding is to the cent, half away from zero.
Examples: HoldingValue
| Shares     | Price    | Value    | Notes                          |
| 100        | 123.4500 | 12345.00 |                                |
| 0          | 123.4500 | 0.00     | A closed position              |
| 100        | 0        | 0.00     | Unpriced                       |
| 12.345678  | 100.0000 | 1234.57  | Rounded up to the cent         |
| 12.344444  | 100.0000 | 1234.44  | Rounded down                   |
| 3          | 0.3333   | 1.00     | 0.9999 rounds to one           |

Attributes HoldingValue
| Attribute | Type   | Default |
| Shares    | Shares | 0       |
| Price     | Price  | 0       |
| Value     | Money  | 0.00    |
| Notes     | String | none    |

Scenario The balance of a brokerage account is its cash and its holdings
Description The brokerage account itself is a placeholder, so its balance is the
# roll-up of the cash account and the holdings beneath it, which is
# the ordinary rule from Accounts and needs nothing special here.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 110.0000 | 2024-06-28 |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | BRK.B  | 10     | 405.0000 | 2024-06-28 |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination             | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2024-01-02 | Equity:Opening Balances | 2500.00  |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-01-03 | Equity:Opening Balances | 11000.00 |
| T3  | Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | 2024-01-03 | Equity:Opening Balances | 4050.00  |
Then rolled up balances are : RolledUpBalance
| Account                | OwnBalance | TotalBalance | Notes            |
| Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2500.00    | 2500.00      | Uninvested cash  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 11000.00   | 11000.00     | 100 at 110.00    |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | 4050.00    | 4050.00      | 10 at 405.00     |
| Assets:Brokerage       | 0.00       | 17550.00     | Cash and holdings |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Buying and selling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Attributes TradeEntry
Description What is typed to record a trade.
| Attribute | Type        | Default    |
| Account   | AccountPath |            |
| Date      | Date        | 2024-01-01 |
| Symbol    | Symbol      |            |
| Shares    | Shares      | 0          |
| Price     | Price       | 0          |
| Fee       | Money       | 0.00       |
| Proceeds  | Money       | 0.00       |

Scenario Buying shares moves cash into the holding
Description Two transactions, and no gain to compute. The holding is carried at
# what was paid for it until a price is recorded.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 0      | 0     | 2024-01-01 |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount         | Date       | Destination             | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash | 2024-01-02 | Equity:Opening Balances | 20000.00 |
When shares bought : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date    | 2024-02-01             |
| Symbol  | VTSAX                  |
| Shares  | 100                    |
| Price   | 100.0000               |
Then transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination           | Amount   |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-02-01 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash | 10000.00 |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-02-01 |

# Left $WIP: "Given transactions are as previous" establishes nothing -- this
# file's Background only inlines a real chart of accounts, never a real
# transactions table, and no earlier step in this scenario gives one either. So
# the ledger holds zero transactions when "shares bought" runs, and the new
# purchase becomes T1, not the T2 the Then table below expects. The Then
# table reads as if it continues the transactions of "Buying shares moves cash
# into the holding" (which does have a real T1), but "as previous" does not
# reach across scenarios -- see the "Never write 'as previous'" rule in
# CLAUDE.md. Either this scenario needs its own explicit "Given transactions
# are" table (most likely with a T1 opening balance, as the sibling
# scenarios all have), or the Then table's Ref needs to read T1; that is a
# decision for the spec's author, not a glue fix.
$WIP
Scenario A commission is an expense, not part of the holding
Description Folding the fee into the value of the holding would make the
# invariant false, because the shares did not cost more than their
# price. It is a three-transaction transaction.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | BRK.B  | 0      | 0     | 2024-01-01 |
Given transactions are as previous
When shares bought : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B |
| Date    | 2024-02-01             |
| Symbol  | BRK.B                  |
| Shares  | 10                     |
| Price   | 400.0000               |
| Fee     | 6.95                   |
Then transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination | Amount  |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | 2024-02-01 | Split       | 4000.00 |
Then split lines are : TransactionSplit
| Destination              | Amount   |
| Expenses:Investment:Fees | 6.95     |
| Assets:Brokerage:Cash    | -4006.95 |

Scenario Buying more shares averages the price, because no lots are kept
Description This is the simplification. Two purchases at different prices leave
# one holding at one price, and that price is the carrying value
# divided by the shares. It is not a cost basis and is not used as
# one: the 1099 has the basis.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-02-01 |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination             | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2024-01-02 | Equity:Opening Balances | 20000.00 |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-02-01 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash   | 10000.00 |
When shares bought : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date    | 2024-03-01             |
| Symbol  | VTSAX                  |
| Shares  | 50                     |
| Price   | 120.0000               |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 150    | 106.6667 | 2024-03-01 |
Then balances are : AccountBalance
| Account                | RawBalance | DisplayBalance | Notes                   |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 16000.00   | 16000.00       | 10000.00 plus 6000.00   |

BusinessRule How the carried price changes when more shares are bought
Description The new price is the total carried value divided by the total shares,
# rounded to four places. The value is the sum of what was paid; the
# price is derived from it, so the invariant holds.
Examples: AveragePrice
| HeldShares | HeldValue | BoughtShares | BoughtPrice | NewShares | NewValue | NewPrice | Notes               |
| 100        | 10000.00  | 50           | 120.0000    | 150       | 16000.00 | 106.6667 |                     |
| 0          | 0.00      | 100          | 100.0000    | 100       | 10000.00 | 100.0000 | A first purchase    |
| 100        | 10000.00  | 100          | 100.0000    | 200       | 20000.00 | 100.0000 | Same price          |
| 3          | 100.00    | 1            | 1.0000      | 4         | 101.00   | 25.2500  | Rounds to four places |

Attributes AveragePrice
| Attribute    | Type   | Default |
| HeldShares   | Shares | 0       |
| HeldValue    | Money  | 0.00    |
| BoughtShares | Shares | 0       |
| BoughtPrice  | Price  | 0       |
| NewShares    | Shares | 0       |
| NewValue     | Money  | 0.00    |
| NewPrice     | Price  | 0       |
| Notes        | String | none    |

Scenario Selling shares at the carried price needs no gain
Description The holding is carried at 106.6667 and sold at that price, so the
# cash in equals the value out and there is nothing left over.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 150    | 106.6667 | 2024-03-01 |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination             | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-03-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | 16000.00 |
When shares sold : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date    | 2024-04-01             |
| Symbol  | VTSAX                  |
| Shares  | 50                     |
| Price   | 106.6667               |
Then transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount         | Date       | Destination            | Amount  |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash | 2024-04-01 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 5333.34 |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 106.6666 | 2024-04-01 |
# The price is re-derived from the value that is left, 10666.66 over 100
# shares, rather than carried forward, so the invariant stays exact.

Scenario Selling above the carried price puts the difference to Equity
Description The difference is a market value change, not income, so it does not
# appear in a report of income and expenses. It is also not a realised
# gain for tax: that figure comes on the 1099.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination             | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-03-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | 10000.00 |
When shares sold : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date    | 2024-04-01             |
| Symbol  | VTSAX                  |
| Shares  | 100                    |
| Price   | 130.0000               |
Then transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount         | Date       | Destination | Amount   |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash | 2024-04-01 | Split       | 13000.00 |
Then split lines are : TransactionSplit
| Destination                 | Amount    |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX      | -10000.00 |
| Equity:Market Value Changes | -3000.00  |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 0      | 130.0000 | 2024-04-01 |

Scenario Selling more shares than are held is refused
Description Short positions are not modelled, so this is always either a missing
# purchase or a typing mistake, and both are worth stopping for.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
When shares sold : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date    | 2024-04-01             |
| Symbol  | VTSAX                  |
| Shares  | 150                    |
| Price   | 130.0000               |
Then rejected because : Rejection
| Reason                                        |
| Only 100 shares of VTSAX are held             |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recording a price
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario Recording a new price revalues the holding
Description This is how the balance is kept current, and it is the only thing
# that has to be done regularly for the figures to mean anything.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination             | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-03-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | 10000.00 |
When price recorded : PriceEntry Vertical
| Symbol | VTSAX      |
| Price  | 110.0000   |
| AsOf   | 2024-06-28 |
Then transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination                 | Amount  |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-06-28 | Equity:Market Value Changes | 1000.00 |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 110.0000 | 2024-06-28 |
Then balances are : AccountBalance
| Account                | RawBalance | DisplayBalance | Notes            |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 11000.00   | 11000.00       | 100 at 110.00    |

Attributes PriceEntry
| Attribute | Type   | Default    |
| Symbol    | Symbol |            |
| Price     | Price  | 0          |
| AsOf      | Date   | 2024-01-01 |

# Left $WIP: both "Given holdings are as previous" and "Given transactions are
# as previous" establish nothing -- this file's Background inlines only a
# real chart of accounts, and nothing earlier in this scenario gives a real
# holdings or transactions table either. So when "price recorded" runs there is
# no VTSAX holding to look up at all, and the -1000.00 / 1000.00 in the Then
# table below has nothing to be computed from. The scenario reads as if it
# continues "Recording a new price revalues the holding" just above it (100
# shares at 100.0000, a T1 of 10000.00), but "as previous" does not reach
# across scenarios -- see the "Never write 'as previous'" rule in CLAUDE.md.
# Spelling out the real holdings and transactions tables (and the Then Ref,
# which would then be T2) is a decision for the spec's author, not a glue
# fix.
$WIP
