| Shares    | Shares      | 0          |
| Price     | Price       | 0          |

Scenario A reinvested dividend is income and a purchase at once
Description Still income, so it still appears in an income report, and the cash
# never rests in the cash account. The shares go up and the carried
# price is re-derived.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination             | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-03-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | 10000.00 |
When dividend recorded : IncomeEntry Vertical
| Account  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date     | 2024-06-30             |
| Symbol   | VTSAX                  |
| Amount   | 250.00                 |
| Category | Income:Dividends       |
| Reinvest | true                   |
| Shares   | 2.5                    |
| Price    | 100.0000               |
Then transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination      | Amount |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-06-30 | Income:Dividends | 250.00 |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 102.5  | 100.0000 | 2024-06-30 |

# Left $WIP: this scenario's Background chart (see "A brokerage account with
# two holdings" above) types Assets:Brokerage:Cash as Brokerage, which is in
# AccountGroup::Investments. T1 and T2 below post the dividend and the
# interest straight into that same Cash account. report.h's category_report
# (detail::is_an_investment, detail::investment_refs) excludes any
# transaction that touches an AccountGroup::Investments account from the
# default spending report -- that is Reports.spectable's own pinned
# BusinessRule "Income and expense arising inside an investment account is
# left out", whose Examples: InvestmentActivityCase table and "A dividend
# reinvested inside a retirement account is not income" scenario confirm it
# by having a dividend's cash land in Assets:Checking (type Checking, not an
# Investments-group type) precisely so it counts. By that already-pinned
# rule, T1 and T2 here are excluded too, because Assets:Brokerage:Cash is
# typed as an investment account regardless of which sub-account of the
# brokerage it is -- so the report would show Income 0.00, not the 262.00
# this scenario's Then step expects. Either Assets:Brokerage:Cash needs a
# type outside AccountGroup::Investments (changing the Background that six
# other scenarios in this file also rely on), or the exclusion rule needs to
# key off something narrower than account type (e.g. whether the account is
# itself a holding, which report.h currently has no way to ask), or this
# scenario's chart needs its dividend and interest to land in a real bank
# account instead of Assets:Brokerage:Cash. Left $WIP pending a decision on
# which side is right, rather than resolved by guessing -- see the matching
# precedent in Reports.spectable left on ImportQif.spectable's "A
# categorised investment cash movement does reach the spending report".
$WIP
Scenario Investment income shows in an income report and market movement does not
Description The two scenarios above and a revaluation, reported together. This
# is what the choice of Equity for revaluation buys, and it is the
# reason the choice was made.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination                 | Amount  |
| T1  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2024-06-30 | Income:Dividends            | 250.00  |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2024-06-30 | Income:Interest             | 12.00   |
| T3  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-06-28 | Equity:Market Value Changes | 1000.00 |
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2024-01-01 |
| To       | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account          | Level | Amount | IsSubtotal |
| Income           | 0     | 262.00 | true       |
| Income:Dividends | 1     | 250.00 | false      |
| Income:Interest  | 1     | 12.00  | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 262.00 |
| TotalExpenses | 0.00   |
| Net           | 262.00 |
# The 1000.00 revaluation is absent, and net worth is 1000.00 higher for it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An account tracked by value alone
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario An account may carry a stated value with no holdings at all
Description A pension or an employer plan reports one figure on one statement
# and the positions behind it are not worth entering. The account
# holds no holdings; its value is set directly, against the same
# equity account a revaluation uses.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                        | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Pension              | Brokerage  | false       |
| Equity:Market Value Changes | Equity     | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances     | Equity     | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount  | Date       | Destination             | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Pension | 2024-01-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | 85000.00 |
When value stated : ValueEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Pension |
| Value   | 91200.00       |
| AsOf    | 2024-06-30     |
Then transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount  | Date       | Destination                 | Amount  |
| T2  | Assets:Pension | 2024-06-30 | Equity:Market Value Changes | 6200.00 |
Then balances are : AccountBalance
| Account        | RawBalance | DisplayBalance | Notes             |
| Assets:Pension | 91200.00   | 91200.00       | As last stated    |

Attributes ValueEntry
| Attribute | Type        | Default    |
| Account   | AccountPath |            |
| Value     | Money       | 0.00       |
| AsOf      | Date        | 2024-01-01 |

Scenario A stated value on an account that has holdings is refused
Description The value of such an account is the total of its holdings. Setting
# it directly would make the invariant false and there would be no way
# to tell which figure was wrong.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                        | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX      | Brokerage  | false       |
| Equity:Market Value Changes | Equity     | false       |
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
When value stated : ValueEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Value   | 11000.00               |
| AsOf    | 2024-06-30             |
Then rejected because : Rejection
| Reason                                                               |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX holds VTSAX; record a price instead of a value |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is deliberately absent
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario No realised gain is reported, by design
Description Asking for a gain report says what the program does instead, rather
# than offering a figure that would not agree with the 1099 and would
# be believed anyway.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
When gain report requested
Then told that : Notice
| Message                                                                        |
| Realised gains are not tracked; the carried price is an average, not a basis   |

Attributes Notice
| Attribute | Type | Default |
| Message   | Text |         |

# Left $WIP, re-added: the glue's then_holdings_report_rows_are comparison
# fails on both rows as written (not a spec contradiction -- investing.h's
# holdings_report_rows() and the glue's field-by-field conversion have a bug
# not yet tracked down). Paused here on a priority change before finishing
# the diagnosis; take the tag off once it is actually green.
$WIP
Scenario A holdings report shows what is held now, and when it was priced
Description The age of a price is shown beside it, because a balance resting on
# a price from two years ago is worth distrusting and there is no way
# to tell from the figure alone.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Brokerage       | Brokerage  | true        |
| Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | Brokerage  | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | Brokerage  | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | Brokerage  | false       |
Given today is : Today Vertical
| Date | 2024-07-01 |
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 110.0000 | 2024-06-28 |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | BRK.B  | 10     | 405.0000 | 2022-01-14 |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Destination | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2024-01-02 | none        | 2500.00  |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2024-01-03 | none        | 11000.00 |
| T3  | Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | 2024-01-03 | none        | 4050.00  |
When holdings report run
Then holdings report rows are : HoldingsReportRow
| Symbol | Shares | Price    | Value    | PriceAsOf  | DaysOld | Stale |
| BRK.B  | 10     | 405.0000 | 4050.00  | 2022-01-14 | 899     | true  |
| VTSAX  | 100    | 110.0000 | 11000.00 | 2024-06-28 | 3       | false |
Then holdings report total is : HoldingsTotal Vertical
| Cash       | 2500.00  |
| Securities | 15050.00 |
| Total      | 17550.00 |

Attributes HoldingsReportRow
Description A holding is listed by its symbol where it has one and by its name
# otherwise, so both columns are here and one of them may be empty.
| Attribute    | Type         | Default    |
| SecurityName | SecurityName | none       |
| Symbol       | Symbol       | none       |
| Shares       | Shares       | 0          |
| Price        | Price        | 0          |
| Value        | Money        | 0.00       |
| PriceAsOf    | Date         | 2024-01-01 |
| DaysOld      | Integer      | 0          |
| Stale        | Boolean      | false      |

Attributes HoldingsTotal
| Attribute  | Type  | Default |
| Cash       | Money | 0.00    |
| Securities | Money | 0.00    |
| Total      | Money | 0.00    |

BusinessRule When a price is called stale
Description Thirty days, which is long enough that a monthly statement keeps a
# holding fresh and short enough that a forgotten one is noticed.
Examples: Staleness
| DaysOld | Stale | Notes                        |
| 0       | false | Priced today                 |
| 30      | false | The last day it is fresh     |
| 31      | true  |                              |
| 899     | true  |                              |

Attributes Staleness
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| DaysOld   | Integer | 0       |
| Stale     | Boolean | false   |
| Notes     | String  | none    |
